Looking at the shape (a zigzag of four squares), I need to find which labeled piece matches a region of the 5×5 grid, allowing rotations by 90° and flipping.

Checking each option against every possible cut position (in all allowed orientations), only piece (A) — with the inverted club and left‑pointing heart on the top row, and the diamond and heart on the bottom row — corresponds exactly to a piece cut from the grid (the symbols' orientations line up correctly after the allowed rotation/flipping). The other options each contain at least one symbol or symbol orientation that cannot appear in that configuration from the grid.

\boxed{A}
